  "id": "DrugBank_DB11964 - MONDO_6896",
  "verbalization": "Ilaprazole is associated with Peptic Esophagitis through a mechanistic pathway involving the indication of Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease (GERD) and its subsequent link to Camostat, which in turn is linked to Peptic Esophagitis. The evidence suggests that Ilaprazole may be repurposed for the treatment of Peptic Esophagitis, as it is indicated for GERD, a condition that is closely linked to Peptic Esophagitis. The shared indication of Camostat in both pathways supports a potential mechanism where Ilaprazole could influence the pathophysiology of GERD, potentially leading to the development of Peptic Esophagitis. The presence of a direct indication from Ilaprazole to Peptic Esophagitis, though not explicitly stated, is inferred through the indirect pathway involving Camostat. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Ilaprazole in modulating GERD-related processes, which may contribute to the development of Peptic Esophagitis. The evidence is supported by a consistent chain of indications, suggesting a plausible biological mechanism that could underlie the repurposing of Ilaprazole for this condition.",
